# TT.TICKET_INTERFACE -- related tickets and related MC files: add_related_ticket
# (S-TICKET-042: both-exist/equal-ids early return, duplicate relation swallowed),
# remove_related_ticket (S-TICKET-043: direction matters, zero matches is a silent no-op),
# add_related_file (S-TICKET-044: the three-way join doubles as the same-company guard --
# a cross-company pairing is refused via NO_DATA_FOUND, swallowed), remove_related_file
# (S-TICKET-045: COUNT then display-name lookup; orphaned file id swallowed).
#
# KNOWN DIFFERENCE (known.diff): step 13 detaches a relation whose file is released only
# to ANOTHER company. Oracle deletes the relation and writes the 100019 event; the
# translation deliberately refuses (DEVIATION(ORACLE-BUG), spec S-TICKET-060 -- the
# same-company guard of add_related_file made symmetric). The expected diff body is the
# missing ticket2mc_file row on Oracle and the missing 100019 event on PostgreSQL.
#
# ORA_USER=system: the fixtures insert into stop.company, stop.contact, mss.host,
# mss.service, mss.host2service and mc.mc_file/mc.mc_file_release; TT holds only SELECT on
# those. Everything is rolled back at the end (COMMITS=no).
ORA_USER=system
COMMITS=no
COMPARE_MSG=no
DESCRIPTION=add/remove_related_ticket and add/remove_related_file on tickets 954010-954012; cross-company detach is the S-TICKET-060 known difference
